WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.660
With my colleague Kurt Konhauser

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.571
at University
of Alberta I have been proposing

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.200
with working with 13 other members

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.280
a program called Light
to Life

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.459
which is the evolution of life based

00:00:12.459 --> 00:00:13.459
on photosynthesis.

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:18.289
So how did it come to be that an organism
figured out how to use the light from the

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:22.509
sun to make chemical bonds that could feed
you?

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:25.010
That's the essence of what this problem is.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.099
We don't understand the evolution of this
process.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:34.100
Photosynthesis was a major driver and it was
all microbial in how it came to be.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.239
And so that's what we're trying to do, taking
these molecules and not worrying about the

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:41.460
sequences, looking at the structures and seeing
if we could find the Legos that were the original

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.320
Legos and that was added on, and what was
added on after that, and what was added on after.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.640
The problem is very, very inter-disciplinary
so we have physical chemists, we have molecular

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:54.379
biologists, we have geochemists, we have geologists,
structural biologists.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:01:01.219
CIFAR allows us to have a very, very broad
group that can interact and potentially then

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:06.620
peel off into smaller groups that can generate
funds for physical research in laboratories

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.040
or in the field.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:14.740
If we had an understanding of how photosynthesis
evolved we could potentially use that to derive

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.930
molecules that could split water without biology.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.570
So there's a natural economy based on electrons,
and there's a human economy based on money

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:29.100
and what I want to do is try to couple them
better so that the human economy can be based

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.460
upon the natural economy of solar energy splitting
water which is going to be a [INAUDIBLE] problem.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.140
[Music]

